# Shell scripts are run inside Linux containers from a bind mount of the checkout, so they
# must reach the container with LF endings whatever the machine that cloned them does. Git
# for Windows converts text to CRLF on checkout by default, and a CRLF script fails in sh on
# its first line — "set: illegal option -" — so the nightly backup would never have run on a
# host administered from a Windows clone, and would have said so only to whoever read the
# timer's log.
*.sh text eol=lf
